option {:value "350067"} "50 kilometres (Mass Start, Freestyle), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350068"} "30 kilometres Skiathlon, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350069"} "4 × 10 kilometres Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350070"} "Team Sprint (Classical), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "350075"} "Sprint (Freestyle), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350087"} "10 kilometres (Classical), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350088"} "30 kilometres (Mass Start, Freestyle), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350089"} "15 kilometres Skiathlon, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350090"} "4 × 5 kilometres Relay, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "350091"} "Team Sprint (Classical), Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "2092"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "2135"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "923555"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000265"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019700"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000120"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/182"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Sprint (Freestyle), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "11 February 2014"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/889"} "Kompleks Dlya Sorevnovaniy Po Lyzhnym Gonkam i Biatlonu Laura, Mountain Cluster, Krasnaya Polyana"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/350054"} "86 from 40 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Final standings based on time achieved in last round competed in."]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Course Length: 1,800 m" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 35 m" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 32 m" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 62 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "In an event renowned for clashes affecting the final outcome, this was no exception. In the qualification round, Norwegian sprint specialist " [:a {:href "/athletes/110932"} "Ola Vigen Hattestad"] " was the fastest skier, and proceeded to win both his quarter-final and semi-final heats skiing from the front. The most prominent drop-outs in the earlier rounds were Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/127933"} "Federico Pellegrino"] ", skiathlon gold medallist " [:a {:href "/athletes/118753"} "Dario Cologna"] " from Switzerland and Norway’s 2010 multiple medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/118832"} "Petter Northug, Jr."] ", who made another disappointing appearance after a virus infection earlier in the year."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final, Hattestad followed his usual tactics, leading from an early stage, followed closely by Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/119956"} "Teodor Peterson"] ". The second Swede, " [:a {:href "/athletes/118779"} "Emil Jönsson"] " was already lagging far behind after an early fall, when three other leading skiers " [:a {:href "/athletes/118802"} "Marcus Hellner"] ", also from Sweden, Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/128192"} "Anders Gløersen"] ", and the Russian home crowd favorite, " [:a {:href "/athletes/128329"} "Sergey Ustyugov"] " were involved in a collision. Gløersen fell on a downhill curve, bringing down with him Ustyugov and Hellner. In the race for gold and silver, Hattestad stayed out of trouble and beat Peterson from the front position by 1.22 sec. Behind them, the already written off Jönsson took advantage of the crashes, and crossed the finish line 20 seconds behind the winner to claim an unexpected bronze."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "QF"] 